---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { FIRM } from '../config';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Notice | Kanon Tax & Advisory"
  description="How Kanon Tax & Advisory collects, uses, protects, and shares client information, including our privacy notice under the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act."
  h1="Privacy notice"
  lede={`Last updated ${FIRM.legalUpdated}`}
  crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]}
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:24px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Tax preparers are treated as financial institutions under the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act, so this
          notice serves two purposes: it is our GLBA privacy notice to clients, and it explains what
          happens to information collected through this website.
        </p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect nonpublic personal information about you from these sources:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>From you</strong> — on organizers, engagement letters, and in conversation: identifying information, taxpayer identification numbers, dates of birth, marital and dependent information, income, deductions, and financial account information</li>
          <li><strong>From your documents</strong> — W-2s, 1099s, K-1s, brokerage and equity award statements, closing documents, and prior-year returns</li>
          <li><strong>From third parties you authorize</strong> — your attorney, financial adviser, prior preparer, or payroll provider</li>
          <li><strong>From this website</strong> — the name, email, phone number, and message you submit through the contact form, plus standard server and analytics data such as IP address and browser type</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          To prepare and file returns, perform the advisory or bookkeeping work you engaged us for,
          communicate with you, meet our own recordkeeping and professional obligations, and protect
          against fraud.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not use or disclose your tax return information for any purpose other than preparing your
          return without your prior written consent, as required by Internal Revenue Code section 7216.
          Where a use requires that consent, we will ask for it separately and specifically.
        </p>

        <h2>What we share, and with whom</h2>
        <p><strong>We do not sell your information. We do not share it with anyone for their own marketing.</strong></p>
        <p>We disclose information only:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>To taxing authorities, as necessary to file your returns or represent you</li>
          <li>To service providers who help us deliver our services — our tax software, encrypted document portal, and e-file transmitter — each of which is contractually bound to protect it and use it only for that purpose</li>
          <li>To people you specifically authorize in writing, such as your attorney, lender, or financial adviser</li>
          <li>Where required by law, subpoena, or a professional standards body</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Because we do not share your information with nonaffiliated third parties for their own use,
          there is no sharing for you to opt out of. If that ever changes, we will notify you and give
          you the opportunity to opt out before it takes effect.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect it</h2>
        <p>
          We maintain a written information security program with administrative, technical, and physical
          safeguards, as required by the FTC Safeguards Rule. In practice that includes encryption of
          client data in transit and at rest, multi-factor authentication on systems that hold client
          information, access limited to those who need it, and an encrypted client portal for exchanging
          documents.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please do not send Social Security numbers, account numbers, or tax documents by email or
          through the website contact form. Use the portal.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We retain client records for at least seven years, consistent with professional standards and
          the periods during which returns may be examined or amended. Website inquiries that do not
          become engagements are retained for a shorter period and then deleted.
        </p>

        <h2>Former clients</h2>
        <p>
          If you stop being a client, we continue to handle your information as described in this notice.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You may request a copy of the information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, and withdraw
          an authorization you previously gave — though some records we are professionally or legally
          required to keep. To make a request, email us.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses no advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. Any analytics we run is limited to
          aggregate traffic measurement, and you can block it in your browser without affecting the site.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We will post any change to this notice here and update the date above. Clients also receive this
          notice at the start of an engagement and annually thereafter.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this notice? Reach us through <a href="/contact/">our contact page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
